content.strength_and_weaknesses:
+ The main idea of enforcing large margin sounds plausible;

+ the margin-enhanced objective term seems effective, as demonstrated by the experimental results (Table 2 & Figure 3). 

- Nevertheless, there is a serious flaw that may render the proposed method useless. 

a) the model in question may be vulnerable to ambiguity attacks, with which even if a legitimate model may also be declared as a copied & extracted model (see Fan et. al. 2019 for successful ambiguity attacks);  

b) Without proving that the proposed method is immune to ambiguity attacks, the watermark detection accuracies in Table 2 is meaningless.

I'd recommend a major revision to include more experimental reuslts and justify the effectiveness of the proposed method in the presence of ambiguity attacks.

